#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:1
msgid "llvm-strings - print strings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:6
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:8
msgid "{program}`llvm-strings` \\[*options*\\] \\[*input...*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:10
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:12
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-strings` is a tool intended as a drop-in replacement for "
"GNU's {program}`strings`, which looks for printable strings in files and "
"writes them to the standard output stream. A printable string is any "
"sequence of four (by default) or more printable characters. A printable "
"character is tab, or any character that is not a control character. The end "
"of the file, or any unprintable byte sequence, terminates the current "
"sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:19
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-strings` looks for strings in each `input` file specified. "
"Unlike GNU {program}`strings` it looks in the entire input file, regardless "
"of file format, rather than restricting the search to certain sections of "
"object files. If \"`-`\" is specified as an `input`, or no `input` is "
"specified, the program reads from the standard input stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:25
msgid "EXAMPLE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:37
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:40
msgid "Silently ignored. Present for GNU {program}`strings` compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:44
msgid ""
"Set the minimum number of printable characters required for a sequence to be "
"considered a string. The default value is 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:47
msgid ""
"The option name `--bytes` dates back to when only single-byte characters "
"were supported. Despite the name, the option value always specifies the "
"number of characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:53
msgid "Specifies the encoding of the input file. Valid arguments are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:54
msgid "`s` (ASCII)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:55
msgid "`S` (current locale's character set)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:56
msgid "`utf8` (UTF-8) The default is `--encoding=S`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:61
msgid "Display a summary of command line options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:65
msgid "Display the name of the containing file before each string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:67
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strings.md:88
